---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const tag = 'v0.1.3';
const baseFor = (t) => `https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-ide/releases/download/${t}/`;
const base = baseFor('v0.1.3');
const builds = [
  { platform: 'macOS, Apple silicon', file: 'rce-ide-0.1.3-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz', size: '16.0 MB', tag: 'v0.1.3', status: 'Ad-hoc signed, not notarized. Binary only.', sha: '6b76de8e19a741c7edabb5f9ab630025e41531fa1d4d72f5f915e2696224310c' },
  { platform: 'Linux x86_64 (glibc 2.39 or later)', file: 'rce-ide-0.1.3-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz', size: '19.5 MB', tag: 'v0.1.3', status: 'Binary only.', sha: '4c55b98b02a3cebd8f60444ba3fc73e1596379d3514a7952264e0df22d74dbed' },
  { platform: 'photon source (MPL-2.0)', file: 'photon-source-mpl-2.0.tar.gz', size: '0.1 MB', tag: 'v0.1.3', status: 'Source of the vendored photon library, offered under its MPL-2.0 license.', sha: 'dee57c47e3f525dde678b2364ad576da60de43e949b7f6ecaa786c6604370c8c' },
  { platform: 'Linux aarch64 (glibc 2.28+), version 0.1.2', file: 'rce-ide-0.1.2-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz', size: '11.4 MB', tag: 'v0.1.2', status: 'The last release for this platform. Cross-built. Not yet run on this hardware. Binary only.', sha: '8f23fd7f5f8dcef42c9ce150c56910d15d7018ec9e7b29aa7379889617a165e0' },
  { platform: 'Windows x86_64, version 0.1.2', file: 'rce-ide-0.1.2-x86_64-pc-windows-gnu.zip', size: '44.4 MB', tag: 'v0.1.2', status: 'The last release for this platform. Cross-built. Not yet run on Windows. Binary only.', sha: 'a66003bce0affb1d84dcb7857d038085e95f3d9fa5fe132fefab9543c10ca1b0' },
];
const repos = [
  { name: 'openIE-dev/rce', href: 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce', deck: 'The language specification, the Lean proofs, the reference checker and the browser playground.' },
  { name: 'openIE-dev/rce-book', href: 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-book', deck: 'A book that teaches RCE step by step.' },
  { name: 'openIE-dev/rce-examples', href: 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-examples', deck: 'Worked example programs.' },
  { name: 'openIE-dev/tree-sitter-rce', href: 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/tree-sitter-rce', deck: 'A tree-sitter grammar for syntax highlighting in editors.' },
  { name: 'openIE-dev/rce-ide', href: 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-ide', deck: 'Source of the RCE IDE agent layer, the language server and the MCP server, as of the 0.1.2 snapshot. Releases from 0.1.3 are binary only.' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Download RCE and the RCE IDE"
  description="Downloads for the RCE IDE 0.1.3 on macOS and Linux x86_64 (0.1.2 for Linux arm64 and Windows), the public RCE repositories, and steps to verify and install. The repository source is licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; the IDE releases are binary only."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">research.openie.dev / rce</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">Download RCE and the RCE IDE</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      RCE (the Reality Code Engine) is a language in which a program is written once as a checked state machine and code in other languages is generated from it.
      The RCE IDE bundles the editor, the checker, a language server and an MCP server. The specification, the Lean library, the reference checker, the book, the examples and the standard host libraries are public source under MIT OR Apache-2.0. The IDE release archives are prebuilt binaries only: from 0.1.2 on, they are built from a private engine and the source in the rce-ide repository is the 0.1.2 snapshot. The archives are free to download.
      The research behind it is in <a href="/papers/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">the RCE paper</a>.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li>Write a program once and generate it in Rust, Python, JavaScript or Scala; the Scala output does not yet agree with the reference.</li>
      <li>The checker rejects broken input before anything runs.</li>
      <li>Download, check the file against its published hash, then unpack and run.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Try it in the browser</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The <a href="https://openie-dev.github.io/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">RCE playground</a> runs the reference checker, compiled to WebAssembly, in your browser.
      Type a program and see whether it is accepted, which rule it breaks, and the trace of each <code>example</code>. Nothing is installed and nothing is sent to a server.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">RCE IDE {tag}</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Release notes: <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-ide/releases/tag/v0.1.3" class="text-brand-cyan">github.com/openIE-dev/rce-ide/releases/tag/v0.1.3</a>.
      Each archive contains <code>rce-ide</code>, <code>rce</code> (the checker), <code>rce-lsp</code>, <code>rce-mcp</code>, the README and the license files.
      The specification draft a build implements is printed by <code>rce --version</code>. There is one language: the specification at one commit (2.7), with no per-module version selection.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 list-none p-0 m-0">
      {builds.map((b) => (
        <li class="glass-card p-5 md:p-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-2">{b.platform} · {b.size}</p>
          <a href={baseFor(b.tag) + b.file} class="font-mono text-sm text-brand-cyan break-all">{b.file}</a>
          <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">{b.status}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-brand-gray break-all">SHA-256 {b.sha}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate">
      All hashes for 0.1.3 in one file: <a href={base + 'SHA256SUMS'} class="font-mono text-brand-cyan">SHA256SUMS</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Verify and install</h2>
    <ol class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3">
      <li>Download the archive for your platform and <code>SHA256SUMS</code> into the same folder.</li>
      <li>Check the hash. If the file was changed or damaged in transit, this step fails.
        <pre class="mt-2 p-3 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-xs"><code>sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing     # Linux
shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing # macOS</code></pre>
        On Windows, run <code>Get-FileHash .\rce-ide-0.1.2-x86_64-pc-windows-gnu.zip</code> in PowerShell and compare the result with the line in <code>SHA256SUMS</code>.
      </li>
      <li>Unpack it: <code>tar xzf rce-ide-&lt;version&gt;-&lt;platform&gt;.tar.gz</code>, or extract the zip on Windows.</li>
      <li>Run <code>./rce-ide</code> to open the editor, or <code>./rce --version</code> and <code>./rce</code> (the list of commands) for the command-line checker.</li>
      <li>macOS only: the binaries are ad-hoc signed and not notarized by Apple, so Gatekeeper may block them. After checking the hash, clear the quarantine flag in the unpacked folder:
        <pre class="mt-2 p-3 overflow-x-auto font-mono text-xs"><code>xattr -d com.apple.quarantine rce rce-ide rce-lsp rce-mcp</code></pre>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Known limits</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li>The Linux aarch64 and Windows builds were cross-built and have not been run on that hardware. Reports of success or failure are welcome as GitHub issues.</li>
      <li>The Linux x86_64 build was smoke-tested without a physical GPU.</li>
      <li>The macOS build is not notarized.</li>
      <li>The IDE archives are binary only. The source for 0.1.3 is not published, so a 0.1.3 binary cannot be rebuilt from public repositories.</li>
      <li>The 0.1.2 archives have their own <a href={baseFor('v0.1.2') + 'SHA256SUMS'} class="text-brand-cyan">SHA256SUMS</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">Source repositories</h2>
    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 list-none p-0 m-0">
      {repos.map((r) => (
        <li class="glass-card p-5">
          <a href={r.href} class="font-mono text-sm text-brand-cyan">{r.name}</a>
          <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">{r.deck}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl text-brand-white">License</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The source in the public RCE repositories and in the rce-ide repository (the 0.1.2 snapshot) is licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option. The binary-only IDE archives from 0.1.3 on are built from an engine whose source is not published. Copyright (c) 2026 Open Interface Engineering, Inc (OpenIE).
      The vendored photon library is MPL-2.0, and its source is the <a href={base + 'photon-source-mpl-2.0.tar.gz'} class="text-brand-cyan">photon source download</a>.
      webpki-roots is CDLA-Permissive-2.0. Full notices are in <code>THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt</code> inside each archive.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/rce/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10">Read the RCE paper</a>
      <a href="/rce/spec/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10">RCE spec</a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white">Catalog</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
